Z||000009||Raydar||10-27-2001||08:50 PM||||At one time, someone was going to try to transplant the crankshaft and some other stuff from that engine into a Duke block, in order to end up with a 2.7 or 3.0. Not sure what became of it, though. <BR>Rumor has it that the Duke was based on this engine. At least enough for the guts to interchange. <BR>The Chevy crank won't work in the DIS (87-88) Duke, though. Has to have the timing wheel for the crank-trigger ignition.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Some mornings, it just isn't worth chewing through the restraints.</FONT>||||reg||1
